[i]Version 5.4.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.4.0 🎨UI OVERHAUL: FACTORY OVERVIEW, RESOURCE DISPLAY & GALAXY MAP QOL🎨[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ UPDATE[/b]
[i]This update fixes the Factory Overview tab freezing up and always showing "Running," an offline catch-up bug, and a trade network chat spam issue, then carries the same care into a broader pass: Resource Display and Galaxy Map QoL all got bug fixes and, where it made sense, a visual refresh.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]⏱️ [b]Offline Catch-Up Over-Applied After a Paused Server:[/b] Pausing the server (common in singleplayer) and resuming could apply the same "captains kept working while you were away" catch-up many times in a row instead of once, finishing long fleet commands almost instantly. Catch-up now applies exactly once per pause.
[*]🐛 [b]Trade Network Blockade Spam:[/b] Linking a Headquarters to supply stations through the delivery network could spam "Trade suspended, under blockade" chat messages every second once any linked station sat in an active war zone, no matter what sector you were actually in. A Smuggler governor now correctly bypasses this, matching how it already works for the production-halt blockade check, and the warning shows in the station's own status instead of spamming your chat.
[*]🐛 [b]Factory Overview Always Said "Running":[/b] Fixed a bug where the Status column read the wrong internal value, so it almost always showed a factory as running fine even when it wasn't producing anything at all.
[*]🐛 [b]Factory Overview Freezing During Sieges:[/b] Fixed a bug where a factory caught in an active Cosmic War siege blockade would completely stop updating in the Factory Overview tab, even after the siege ended.
[*]🐛 [b]Newly Claimed Asteroid Mines Not Appearing:[/b] Fixed a bug that could prevent freshly claimed asteroid mines, like Ice Mines, from ever showing up in the Factory Overview tab.
[*]🐛 [b]Tooltip Text Fix:[/b] Fixed the per-factory tooltip occasionally showing untranslated text for non-English players.
[*]🐛 [b]Dedicated Server Reliability:[/b] Fixed a couple of internal issues that could cause Factory Overview to fetch the wrong player's data, or a rare crash risk, specifically on dedicated servers with multiple players.
[*]🐛 [b]Galaxy Map QoL Internal Reliability Pass:[/b] Fixed a deep-seated internal wiring issue that risked the whole Galaxy Map QoL feature silently misbehaving, plus a handful of smaller cleanups. No visible changes, just a more solid foundation.
[/list]

[b]✨IMPROVEMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]🔄 [b]Live Auto-Refresh:[/b] The Factory Overview tab now automatically refreshes itself every 10 seconds while it's open, instead of only updating when you switch tabs or click Refresh.
[*]📊 [b]More Accurate Status Percentages:[/b] The Status column now reflects roughly the last 30 minutes of activity instead of averaging over your whole play session, so a new problem shows up quickly instead of getting buried under hours of good history.
[*]💾 [b]Stats Now Survive Restarts:[/b] Factory Overview's tracking now properly saves and reloads with your game instead of quietly resetting every time a sector unloads or the server restarts.
[*]⚙️ [b]Resource Display Settings Made More Reliable:[/b] Your HUD preferences are now saved through a more robust system under the hood — your existing settings carry over, no action needed.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.3.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.3.1 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets two dedicated server crashes and restores a Station Governor bonus that stopped working.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Dedicated Server Crash on Scout Reports & Station Income:[/b] Fixed two scripts that could crash a dedicated server on startup: the Scout Command dialogue table and the Station Income Manager. Both built a piece of translated text too early, before the server was ready to translate it.
[*]🐛 [b]Merchant Governor Income Bonus Restored:[/b] Found and fixed a duplicate Station Income Manager script. Only one copy was ever actually running, and it was missing the Merchant Governor bonuses (+25% passive station income, +50% AI traffic) that the Wiki and Player Guide have always promised. Consolidated to one script with the bonuses working again, on top of the current War Profiteering and Core Distance income scaling. Also fixed the trade-frequency half of the bonus, which was quietly making trades less frequent instead of more.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.3.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.3.0 🛠️TRASH MANAGER, COMMAND CENTER & FLEET STATUS OVERHAUL!🛠️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY & HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]Three UI features got a real upgrade this patch, alongside the newly overhauled Trash Manager and an internal reliability pass across a wide range of scripts.[/i]

[b]📖 CODEX UPDATED[/b]
[list]
📖[*] Updated Cosmic Overhaul's codex entry with up-to-date information.
[/list]

[b]✨NEW FEATURES[/b]
[list]
[*]🔥 [b]Trash Manager Revamped[/b] Integrated "Trash Manager Revamped" version of the overhaul Trash Man UI.
[*]🎖️ [b]Command Center Tab Rebuilt:[/b] The old Command Center just listed your ships' orders with no way to sort or filter it - and honestly, vanilla's own Fleet window already covered that. It's now a proper Fleet Operations & Earnings Dashboard: track cumulative credits earned from all your background trading/mining/salvaging in one place (with a reset button), instantly see which ships are sitting idle doing nothing, get one-click filters for ships completing soon or recently recalled, and sort the whole list by any column. The layout is also a lot less cramped now.
[*]💹 [b]Factory Overview Tab Enhanced:[/b] Added a Location column so you can see exactly where each factory is without clicking through, and a Status column that shows at a glance whether a factory is running smoothly or stalled out (and why) - no more hovering every single row to find your underperforming factories. There's also a new Totals line up top showing your combined income, expenses, and profit across every factory shown.
[*]🚑 [b]Fleet Status Screen Improved:[/b] Your ship selection lists now show each ship's current hull durability right next to its name, color-coded so a damaged ship jumps out at you, plus a running count of how many ships you have pinned to the HUD. A ship critically low on hull will now pulse on your HUD overlay instead of just sitting there in flat red - much harder to miss while you're busy elsewhere.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Internal Script Reliability Pass:[/b] Cleaned up internal script wiring across 16 files, including the Gates, Equipment Dock, Fighter Merchant, Turret Merchant, Scrapyard, Station Income Management, Fleet Status, Galaxy Map QoL, Command Center, Factory Overview, Player Bulletin Board, Resource Display, and Respawn HUD. This prevents rare event desyncs, double-triggered logic, and cases where a script could silently fall back to a much slower update rate than intended.
[*]🐛 [b]Fleet Status Screen Ship Lists Fixed:[/b] Found and fixed a deeper wiring bug in the Fleet Status Screen (separate from the pass above) that could prevent its two ship-selection lists from populating correctly, plus a crash risk when clicking a ship right as it was renamed, sold, or destroyed.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.2.5[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.2.5 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix directly targets a major issue with the background shipyard production tracker crashing on initialization and duplicating ships infinitely.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Shipyard Infinite Spawning Exploit:[/b] Fixed a critical bug in the background Shipyard Production Tracker where the script would crash trying to initialize vanilla components without the proper dependencies loaded. This crash prevented the tracker from removing the job from the player's queue, resulting in the ship spawning infinitely every time the player re-entered the sector.
[*]🐛 [b]Shipyard Veteran Reconstruction Crash:[/b] Added missing dependencies to ensure that if the player builds a ship on Veteran difficulty or lower, the script can safely hand out the Reconstruction Token without crashing the server.
[*]🐛 [b]Shipyard Null Entity Crash:[/b] Fixed an issue in the Shipyard Production Tracker where restoring a mission with a missing entity pointer would crash the script on load. The tracker now safely verifies entity existence or falls back to generic coordinates, preventing mission corruption upon server restarts.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.2.4[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.2.4 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix directly targets a major issue with the ARCC Offline Simulation not working for Singleplayer and Private Server saves.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]ARCC Offline Catch-up Singleplayer Fix:[/b] Resolved a critical bug where the ARCC offline simulation catch-up would fail to process time elapsed for singleplayer and private server users who completely shut down the game. The issue was caused by Avorion's aggressive early autosave mechanism wiping the player's offline timestamp on startup before the catch-up system could evaluate it. The simulation now strictly safeguards the offline timestamp until the catch-up logic successfully runs.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.2.3[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.2.3 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets UI rendering issues within DLC shops caused by outdated layout overrides. While providing a bugfix for AARC multiplayer sync issues.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Rift Research Center Shop UI:[/b] Fixed an issue where the Rift Research Center shop displayed all data costs as 0 Credits and completely failed to show the player's Xsotan Data inventory. Injected the missing DLC layout elements and dynamic price checks back into the shop overrides to fully restore Vanilla DLC shop functionality while retaining custom pagination.
[*]🐛 [b]ARCC Offline Catch-up Multiplayer Sync:[/b] Fixed a critical issue on multiplayer dedicated servers where the ARCC offline simulation catch-up would fail to trigger when players logged back into a previously empty (paused) server. The system now utilizes a gap-detection mechanism to properly calculate elapsed real-world time during server pauses, ensuring commands correctly progress as if the player was offline.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.2.2[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.2.2 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets a severe issue regarding empty sector generation during Trade Rumors![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Empty Trade Rumor Generation:[/b] Fixed a severe bug where buying a 10,000 Cr "Trade Rumor" from a Smuggler's Market or Casino would simply add an empty coordinate to your map, leading you to nothing but dead space. The event now utilizes Avorion's native engine to algorithmically scan the galaxy map for high-profit secret sectors (Hidden Stashes, Smuggler Hideouts, Scrap Yards) up to 30 sectors away.
[*]🐛 [b]Trade Rumor Map Note:[/b] Added a map note tooltip to the Trade Rumor coordinate, ensuring players no longer lose track of the rumored sector on the galaxy map.
[*]🐛 [b]Shipyard Tracker Overwrite & Deletion:[/b] Fixed critical architecture flaws in the global shipyard production tracker introduced in v5.2.1. The mission script now properly utilizes arrays rather than singletons to securely manage multiple queued ships across the galaxy without overwriting data, and resolves an issue where the mission prematurely deleted itself before the player could retrieve their ships.
[*]🐛 [b]Shipyard Engine Constraints:[/b] Removed illegal global wrapper functions from `shipyard.lua` to prevent namespace shadowing and event desynchronization.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.2.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.2.1 🛠️QOL PATCH UPDATE!🛠️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch introduces a major Quality of Life improvement for player Shipyards![/i]

[b]✨NEW FEATURES[/b]
[list]
[*]🔥 [b]Global Shipyard Production Timers & Map Tracker:[/b] Resolved a vanilla Avorion flaw where queued ships at a Shipyard would indefinitely pause their construction timers if the sector was unloaded by players. Shipyard timers have now been decoupled from the station itself and moved to a global background simulation attached to the player. Furthermore, whenever you queue a ship, a highly visible, silent tracker mission will automatically pinpoint the exact Shipyard sector on your Galaxy Map so you never lose it again! When the background timer finishes, the ship will automatically spawn in the sector regardless of whether you are there or not.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.2.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.2.0 ✨FEATURE UPDATE!✨[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ MINOR EXPANSION PATCH[/b]
[i]This minor update introduces a brand new dynamic economy and multiple Quality of Life features, including Boarding Loot, Trade Route Rumors, Mining Hazard Pay, and an Asteroid Density Rebalance![/i]

[b]✨NEW FEATURES[/b]
[list]
[*]🔥 [b]Smuggler Captain Black Market Bonus:[/b] Trading at Smuggler Markets or Casinos now grants dynamic payouts and discounts when using a Smuggler Captain. The bonus scales from 5% up to 25% based on the captain's Tier (Common to Legendary), and is doubled when trading directly with the Syndicate Boss (Level 5).
[*]🔥 [b]Dynamic Boarding Loot:[/b] Successfully boarding a ship or station will now automatically drop 1-2 high-rarity loot crates into space (Turrets or Upgrades). A small reward for seizing control of enemy vessels!
[*]🔥 [b]Trade Route Rumors (Bartenders):[/b] Bartenders at Smuggler Markets and Casinos now offer a new dialogue option to buy trade route rumors for 10,000 Credits. The rumor reveals the coordinates of a highly profitable sector on your galaxy map!
[*]🔥 [b]Mining Captain Hazard Pay:[/b] When assigning a Mining Captain to a background mining operation, there is a chance the area will contain hazardous conditions (simulated). If the captain encounters a hazard, they automatically secure a 10% bonus to raw ore extraction, representing hazard pay and overtime!
[*]🔥 [b]Asteroid Density Rebalance:[/b] Overhauled the asteroid generation logic. Outer rim sectors now feature fewer but significantly larger asteroids (ideal for manual mining). In contrast, sectors closer to the core now generate highly dense fields of smaller asteroids (perfect for massive fleet operations)!
[*]🔥 [b]Galactic Politics Sabotage:[/b] You can now pay a 5,000,000 Credits bribe to the Smuggler's Market to intentionally lower the relationship between two random NPC factions across the galaxy. This triggers a news broadcast and sparks proxy wars!
[/list]

[i]Version 5.1.4[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.1.4 🐛BUGFIX & BALANCE PATCH UPDATE!⚖️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix revolves around fixing a fatal Boarding Crash, the complete removal of Smart Jump, and a huge Merchant Captain economy rebalance![/i]

[b]🖥️BALANCING[/b]
[list]
[*]⚖️ [b]Merchant Captain Synergy:[/b] The flat 15% discount/bonus payout applied globally when trading with a Merchant Captain has been rebalanced to dynamically scale based on both the captain's level and tier. The new formula adds +2% per level and +2% per tier, creating perfect synergy with the vanilla Captain progression system. A fresh Common Level 1 Merchant now provides a minimal +2% edge, while a Max Level 5 Legendary Merchant pushes the economy to a massive +16% bonus payout and discount!
[/list]

[b]🔧ADJUSTMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]❌ [b]Smart Jump Autopilot:[/b] Completely scrapped the Smart Jump hotkey feature. Attempting to natively hijack the Avorion engine's hyperspace calculation routines and force ship alignments without a captain resulted in engine limitations that proved too drastic for the scope of the Cosmic series.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Sealed Hulk State Exploit:[/b] Fixed an exploit in `sealedhulkboarding.lua` where the script failed to utilize the engine's `secure()` and `restore()` pipeline to save the event state to disk. Players could previously abuse this by pushing deeper into the hulk, logging out, and reloading the sector to reset the event back to the first stage and farm resources indefinitely. The event state is now strictly serialized to the save file.
[*]🐛 [b]Sealed Hulk Boarding Crash:[/b] Fixed a silent engine crash inside `sealedhulkboarding.lua` where choosing the aggressive options ("Blow the blast doors" or "Push through the crossfire") would attempt to execute a `ship:removeCrew` call without the strictly required `Crewman` argument. The boarding logic will now correctly iterate over the ship's crew manifest to simulate realistic casualties without throwing silent C++ exceptions!
[*]🐛 [b]Localization:[/b] Fixed missing server-to-client UI localization tags (`%_T`) on the Sealed Hulk extraction messages.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.1.3[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.1.3 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix resolves a severe background crash preventing asteroids from properly regenerating![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Respawn Resource Asteroids Crash:[/b] Fixed a critical issue where the background simulation would attempt to read the sector's controlling faction incorrectly. This caused the Famine Synergy check to silently crash the sector's asteroid regeneration loop. The script now natively and securely resolves the controlling faction!
[/list]

[i]Version 5.1.2[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.1.2 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets a severe shield regeneration bug linked to Captain Elite Traits![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Elite Captain Shield Stutter:[/b] Fixed a major logic flaw where Elite Captains (Commodore / Scavenger) were continuously applying and removing their status buffs every 5 seconds. This micro-stutter was constantly forcing the game engine to reset the "out of combat" regeneration timer, completely preventing shields from naturally recharging. The buffs now correctly "refresh" instead, allowing shields to recharge normally while the captain is assigned!
[/list]

[i]Version 5.1.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V5.1.1 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix directly addresses two reported bugs causing AI trader crashes and severe UI stat oscillation with Elite Captain traits![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]AI Trader Sector Jump Crash:[/b] Fixed an engine error that caused AI station traders to endlessly crash and spam the console when trying to jump out of the sector. They will now properly calculate their jump trajectories and leave the sector cleanly!
[*]🐛 [b]Elite Captain Buff Stacking & UI Oscillation:[/b] Fixed the background logic for Commodore and Scavenger Elite Traits!
- Fixed an issue where the buffs were applying massively inflated percentages (+110% instead of +10%).
- Fixed a bug where the buffs would overlap every 5 seconds and continuously stack with themselves.
- The Commodore's damage buff now correctly boosts Fire Rate instead of magically inflating your Armed Turret slots!
[/list]

[i]Version 5.1.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V5.1.0 ✨FEATURES & 🪲BUGFIX UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch introduces new features and squashes critical background simulation bugs.[/i]

[b]🔬QUALITY OF LIFE (QoL) UPDATES[/b]
[list]
[*]✨ [b]Consolidate Inventory to Vault:[/b] Added a new button in the Trash Man UI allowing you to instantly transfer all unequipped and non-favorite turrets and subsystems from your private inventory directly into the Alliance Vault.
[*]✨ [b]Smart Jump Orientation Hotkey:[/b] Added a new hotkey (configurable via Cosmic Configuration Menu) that instantly aligns your ship to your plotted hyperspace jump destination, saving you the hassle of manually turning your ship.
[*]✨ [b]Crew Mutiny Fallback Wallet:[/b] Implemented an automated background protection script. If your personal funds run critically low before payday, the system will automatically transfer the missing credits from the Alliance Vault and notify you via chat, preventing a silent crew strike.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Mining Operation Background Crash:[/b] Patched a server crash occurring during background mining operations (`minecommand.lua:attempt to call field MineableBy`). This crash was caused by conflicting mods destroying the vanilla `galaxy.lua` export table. Cosmic Overhaul now injects a universal safeguard that forces the function back into memory, protecting your mining fleets from crashing out.
[*]🐛 [b]Dynamic Reputation Rapid Decay:[/b] Fixed a critical bug where the reputation decay script was missing a namespace declaration and using global wrappers. This caused the Avorion engine to silently fail its 45-minute throttle and fallback to a 15-second loop, applying 45 minutes worth of decay every 15 seconds! Relations will now correctly decay precisely once every 45 minutes as intended.
[*]🐛 [b]Allied Relations Enhancer Crash & Silent Failure:[/b] Patched a fatal engine crash occurring during diplomacy and reputation events. The script was incorrectly attempting to index raw integer IDs directly instead of normalizing them into Faction objects first, which would crash the server. Additionally, fixed a silent failure where the script looked for a non-existent `.alliance` property, completely preventing it from mirroring your reputation changes to your Alliance. It now properly executes the vanilla normalization pipeline and perfectly mirrors your diplomatic actions!
[/list]

[i]Version 5.0.12[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V5.0.12 ⚙️ADJUSTMENTS UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This small patch further refines the dynamic reputation decay to drastically reduce UI notification spam![/i]

[b]🔧ADJUSTMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]⚙️ [b]Dynamic Reputation Pacing:[/b] The dynamic reputation decay interval has been further increased from 15 minutes to 45 minutes. Because the background script mathematically scales the penalty to match the interval, your overall hourly reputation loss remains exactly the same! This drastically reduces UI notification spam by processing 45 minutes worth of decay all at once (e.g. "-5828 Reputation with Cookie Empire").
[/list]

[i]Version 5.0.11[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v5.0.11 ⚖️BALANCING UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch refines the dynamic reputation decay to reduce UI notification spam![/i]

[b]🖥️BALANCING[/b]
[list]
[*]⚙️ [b]Dynamic Reputation Pacing:[/b] The dynamic reputation decay interval has been increased from 60 seconds to 15 minutes. Because the background script mathematically scales the penalty to match the interval, your overall hourly reputation loss remains exactly the same! However, instead of spamming your screen with a tiny "-1 Relation" notification every 60 seconds, it will now cleanly process 15 minutes worth of decay all at once (e.g. "-15 Relations"). This drastically reduces UI notification spam while maintaining the exact same math and balance.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.0.10[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V5.0.10 ⚖️BALANCE, ⚙️ADJUSTMENTS & 🐛BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch addresses several bugs reported, balancing game mechanics and system adjustments.[/i]

[b]🖥️BALANCING[/b]
[list]
[*]⚖️ [b]Subspace Weather Rarity:[/b] Significantly reduced the spawn rate of natural Subspace Weather events (Ion Storms, Solar Flares) to 1% (down from 15%) and massively increased the global cooldown between storms to 4-8 hours (up from 30-60 minutes). Weather events are now a very rare, high-impact phenomenon rather than a constant nuisance.
[*]⚖️ [b]War Profiteering:[/b] Increased the maximum passive income multiplier for Player Stations located in a max-heat Cosmic War zone from 250% to 300%. Setting up supply chains in warzones is now incredibly lucrative.
[*]⚖️ [b]Eclipse Contraband Premium (Cosmic Chronicles Synergy):[/b] Reduced the Smuggler's Market payout multiplier for fencing Ascendant Matter and Eclipse Datacores from 200% (2.0x) to 150% (1.5x) to curb late-game inflation while still offering a solid premium.
[*]⚖️ [b]Ascendancy Trade Fear (Cosmic Ascendancy Synergy):[/b] Increased the flight time penalty for non-smuggler merchants trading near factions at war with the Ascendancy (The Eclipse) from 35% delay (1.35x) to 50% delay (1.5x).
[*]⚖️ [b]Famine Relief Charity:[/b] Increased the reputation multiplier for Charity Missions sent to starving factions from +75% to +100%.
[*]⚖️ [b]War Profiteering Distance Scaling:[/b] Player Station passive income now scales dynamically based on distance to the galactic core. Stations near the edge of the galaxy receive a standard 1.0x multiplier, while stations deep in the core receive up to a 3.0x multiplier to their base payout, heavily incentivizing core expansions.
[/list]

[b]🔧ADJUSTMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]⚙️ [b]Subspace Weather Generator Engine Compliance:[/b] Hardened the structural foundation of the weather generator. It now features full state persistence (storm cooldowns will properly save/restore across server restarts instead of resetting to 0) and strict adherence to the Avorion SectorView API for coordinate parsing.
[*]⚙️ [b]Cosmic Overhaul Codex:[/b] Updated the Codex with new information while adding in left out information from the official Cosmic Overhaul Wiki.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Dynamic Reputation Decay Alliance Double-Penalty:[/b] Fixed a severe logic flaw where passive reputation decay was being calculated independently for both the Player and their Alliance, but applied using an API function (`cvf.changeRelations`) that automatically mirrored the Player's decay to the Alliance. This caused the Alliance to suffer the decay penalty twice. The script now safely bypasses mirroring and applies decay directly via the vanilla `galaxy:setFactionRelations()` API.
[*]🐛 [b]Dynamic Reputation Decay Type Safety:[/b] Added strict `tonumber()` type coercion when fetching interaction timestamps to prevent potential silent Lua exceptions if the engine cache returned a timestamp as a string.
[*]🐛 [b]Dynamic Reputation Decay Entity Script Structure:[/b] Cleaned up the script structure by removing a leaked `return` statement at the bottom of the script that attempted to export undefined globals (a copy-paste error from vanilla's `relations.lua`).
[*]🐛 [b]Famine Event Persistence:[/b] Fixed a critical API bug where the background Famine Listener queue lacked state persistence. Famine debuff evaluations will no longer permanently skip ships if a sector unloads or the server restarts while ships are still waiting in the queue.
[/list]

[i]Version 5.0.9[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]⚙️V5.0.9 HOTFIX PATCH UPDATE!⚙️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This small patch addresses UI keybind overlaps.[/i]
[*]⚙️ [b]Keybind Adjustments:[/b] Unbound the default keys for the Cosmic Overhaul UI tabs (Bulletin Board, Resource Display). They now default to unbound to allow players to set their own custom shortcuts without overlapping with other mods.

[i]Version 5.0.8[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛V5.0.8 BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch addresses severe AI combat disruptions caused by background logic crashes.[/i]
[*]📦 [b]Delivery Missions Logic:[/b] Delivery missions will no longer select a destination sector owned by a faction that the questgiver is currently at war with.
[*]🐛 [b]Dynamic Reputation Decay AI Halt:[/b] Fixed a critical bug in `DynamicReputationDecay.lua` where evaluating non-existent relations caused an `attempt to compare number with nil` exception. This background error would flood the server update loop, severely disrupting faction AI logic and causing ships to ignore combat.

[i]Version 5.0.7[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛V5.0.7 CRITICAL BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ CRITICAL HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch addresses issues with offline simulation and severe AI single sector population.[/i]
[*]🐛 [b]Dynamic Reputation Decay Error:[/b] Fixed a severe server log spam issue originating from `DynamicReputationDecay.lua`. The script was incorrectly passing integer indices directly into the `getFactionRelations` native API, causing recurring `invalid type 'number'` errors. Indices are now properly wrapped in `Faction()` objects.
[*]🐛 [b]Weather Generator Loading:[/b] Fixed a silent script attachment failure in `server.lua`. `co_weather_generator.lua` was missing the mandatory `data/scripts/` root path prefix, preventing the engine from properly loading the global weather script on server start.

[i]Version 5.0.6[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛V5.0.6 BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch addresses issues with offline simulation and severe AI single sector population.[/i]
[*]🐛 [b]Offline Simulation:[/b] Resolved an issue where checking the `Enable Offline Catch-up` option in the CCM window and relaunching the game would result in the option visually or functionally reverting to disabled. The background simulation script now evaluates the configuration dynamically at runtime when parsing the first update tick, rather than caching the default values prematurely during initial script load before the Cosmic Configuration Menu completes parsing `ccm.lua`.

[*]🐛 [b]Traders (AI Bloat & Desync):[/b] Fixed a severe optimization bug originating from the `ft_gateTradeMult` trader influx logic within `factory.lua`. If a player sat in an accelerated sector (e.g., heavily populated with Gates/Wormholes) for an extremely extended period (8+ hours), the factory spawned traders faster than the vanilla Avorion docking AI could process them. Overwhelmed docking queues caused AI tradeship scripts to timeout or detach, leaving hundreds of permanent, unscripted ghost ships drifting thousands of kilometers away and tricking the factory into continuously spawning more. A strict sector-wide safety cap on active AI traders has been introduced to prevent runaway inflation while preserving trade volume.

[i]Version 5.0.5[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛V5.0.5 BUGFIX & BALANCING UPDATE!⚖️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX & GAME BALANCE PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch addresses issues with map commands offline simulation, while balancing a few numbers..[/i]
[*]🐛 [b]Offline Simulation:[/b] Fixed a critical logic error in `simulation.lua` where the script fetched `Server().unpausedRuntime` instead of the system's real-world clock (`os.time()`). Because `unpausedRuntime` freezes while the server is offline or the game is closed, returning players were incorrectly awarded exactly 0 seconds of background catch-up time regardless of how long they were away. This has been fully corrected.
[*]⚖️ [b]Scavenger Yield Buff (Cosmic War):[/b] Increased the Salvage Yield multiplier from `1.20` (+20%) to `1.50` (+50%) when a Scavenger captain is operating inside an active Contested Siege Zone. Risking a captain inside a War Zone is now much more lucrative.
[*]⚖️ [b]Ascendancy Trade Fear (Cosmic Ascendancy):[/b] Increased the flight time penalty for non-smuggler merchants trading near factions actively at war with The Eclipse from `20%` delay to `35%` delay.
[*]⚖️ [b]Charity Reputation Bonus (Cosmic Vault):[/b] Buffed the diplomatic multiplier for Charity Missions sent to starving factions from `+50%` to `+75%`. Sending aid during an economic crisis is now incredibly rewarding.
[*]⚖️ [b]Eclipse Contraband Premium (Cosmic Chronicles):[/b] Buffed the Smuggler's Market fence multiplier for `Ascendant Matter` and `Eclipse Datacore` from `+50%` to `+100%` payout.

[i]Version 5.0.4[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛V5.0.4 BUGFIX & BALANCING UPDATE!⚖️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX & GAME BALANCE PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch addresses lingering issues with transfer crews, cargo and goods, while balancing a few numbers and there.[/i]
[*]🐛 Addressed a lingering edge case in the `v5.0.3` Hangar fix. The server was attempting to resolve the `Hangar` component directly from network-transmitted UUIDs, which could silently fail during transfers between complex entity states (e.g., Alliance ships) and falsely report a "Missing hangar." The engine now securely resolves the component strictly via the verified Entity object instance.
[*]⚖️ Softened the blunt +250% trade bonus applied to all starving factions. It now appropriately scales up based on severity (Struggling: +125%, Resource Starved: +175%, Severe Famine: +250%). Smuggler blockade bypasses natively halve these bonuses.
[*]⚖️ Toned down the extreme stat penalties applied to factions experiencing Severe Famines (Shields: -50%, Velocity: -30%) and Resource Starved (Shields: -30%, Velocity: -20%) to keep AI fleets somewhat competitive when reacting to Cosmic War siege events.
[*]⚖️ Lowered the profit ceiling for fencing stolen Rift Technology at the Smuggler's Market to a random scale of `1.5x - 2.5x` to prevent hyper-inflation of the late-game economy when combined with Smuggler trait bonuses.

[i]Version 5.0.3[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛V5.0.3 BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This very small patch fixes a reported issue regarding hangar and transfer crews![/i]
[*]🐛 Fixed a critical bug in `transfercrewgoods.lua` where the `Entity().hangar` property was incorrectly referenced instead of the proper `Hangar(entity)` component API. This resolved an issue that completely blocked all fighter transfers between ships and stations by falsely claiming a hangar was missing.

